Perfect. Here is the clean workflow.

⸻

✅ Goal
	•	Build Kea 3.0 from source in an Ubuntu Docker container
	•	Container has no internet (fully offline build)
	•	Installation happens later on another EC2 VM

To do offline build you need:
	1.	Ubuntu build container
	2.	Source tarball of Kea (kea-3.0.tar.gz)
	3.	All build dependencies (.deb)

I’ll show two options:

⸻

🟦 OPTION A — If you DO HAVE internet on the build container

(This is easier.)

1. Start the container

docker run -it --name kea-build ubuntu:22.04 bash

2. Install build tools

apt update
apt install -y build-essential git automake libtool pkg-config \
               libboost-all-dev libssl-dev liblog4cplus-dev

3. Copy Kea source into container

On your host:

docker cp kea-3.0.tar.gz kea-build:/tmp/

Inside container:

cd /tmp
tar xvf kea-3.0.tar.gz
cd kea-3.0

4. Build

./configure
make -j$(nproc)
make install DESTDIR=/output

This will produce a folder /output containing:

/output/usr/local/sbin/kea-dhcp4
/output/usr/local/sbin/kea-dhcp6
/output/usr/local/sbin/kea-ctrl-agent
...

5. Copy build output back to your host

docker cp kea-build:/output ./kea-build-output


⸻

🟦 OPTION B — FULLY OFFLINE BUILD (no apt-get inside container)

If you want true offline build, you must prepare a “dependency bundle” before starting the container:

You need to download these .deb files on another machine:
	•	build-essential
	•	automake
	•	libtool
	•	pkg-config
	•	libboost-all-dev
	•	libssl-dev
	•	liblog4cplus-dev
	•	libc6-dev
	•	gcc / g++
	•	make

I can generate an exact list for you if you tell me your Kea version and Ubuntu version (e.g. 22.04, 20.04).

Then:

1. Create the container

docker run -it --name kea-build ubuntu:22.04 bash

2. Copy your dependency bundle

On your host:

docker cp deb-packages/ kea-build:/deps/
docker cp kea-3.0.tar.gz kea-build:/tmp/

3. Install all .deb files offline

In the container:

cd /deps
dpkg -i *.deb

4. Build Kea

Same as before:

cd /tmp
tar xvf kea-3.0.tar.gz
cd kea-3.0
./configure
make -j$(nproc)
make install DESTDIR=/output

5. Export the compiled binaries

docker cp kea-build:/output ./kea-build-output

Then you can copy kea-build-output to your EC2 VM and install manually.

